WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.850
First, let's picture this.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:08.850
How do we usually know if the water in the field is off, or if something is wrong?

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.850
Mostly, we just look at it, right?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.950
But by the time we notice, the rice may already be damaged.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.450
SolarAqua steps in to solve this problem

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.150
with small sensor boxes placed right in the field,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:31.450
powered by solar cells: no plugs, and no frequent battery changes.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.750
This is the main water-quality box.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.750
Inside, we have four sensors:

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.750
a pH sensor,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.750
a turbidity sensor,

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.750
a conductivity sensor,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.750
and a dissolved-oxygen sensor.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:01.550
On top is the solar panel.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.550
Place the box in the middle of the paddy,

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.550
with the solar panel in full sunlight,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.750
and nothing blocking it.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.750
This is the gateway box. It receives data from water-quality boxes 1, 2 and 3.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.750
After powering it on, wait about 1-2 minutes, then press the green button

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.750
to start the system.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.750
The water-quality boxes send their data here, to the gateway.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.750
Then the gateway sends it to the website.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.750
You can view it on a phone or any device,

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.250
and the data updates about every 5 minutes.
